                            <!-- 1. Introduction -->
                            <section id="sec-introduction" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">1. Introduction</h3>
                                <h5 class="mt-3">About Shiv Amruttulya Management System</h5>
                                <p>Welcome to the Shiv Amruttulya Management System! This software is designed specifically to simplify the day-to-day operations of Shiv Amruttulya tea shops and franchises. It helps you manage your business efficiently from anywhere.</p>
                                
                                <h5 class="mt-3">Purpose of the application</h5>
                                <p>The main purpose is to replace manual record-keeping with a secure, digital platform. It centralizes sales collections, expenses, grocery purchases, and franchise management in one easy-to-use dashboard, giving you real-time visibility into your business performance.</p>
                                
                                <h5 class="mt-3">Who should use this application</h5>
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Administrators:</strong> Oversee all shops, franchises, users, and global reports.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Franchise Owners:</strong> Track performance, collections, and expenses for their specific franchise.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Shop Managers:</strong> Enter daily collections, log expenses, and update daily activities.</li>
                                </ul>

                                <h5 class="mt-3">Key benefits</h5>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>Eliminates paper-based errors and missing records.</li>
                                    <li>Provides instant financial reports (profits, expenses, collections).</li>
                                    <li>Easily track which shop is performing best.</li>
                                    <li>Secure access with user roles so staff only see what they need to see.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 2. Getting Started -->
                            <section id="sec-getting-started" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">2. Getting Started</h3>
                                
                                <h5 class="mt-3">Login to the application</h5>
                                <p>Go to the provided login link. Enter your registered <strong>Email Address</strong> and <strong>Password</strong>, then click the "Login" button. If you forget your password, contact your administrator to reset it.</p>
                                
                                <h5 class="mt-3">Dashboard overview</h5>
                                <p>Once logged in, you will land on the Dashboard. This is your command center, showing a quick summary of today's collections, monthly trends, and overall business health at a single glance.</p>
                                
                                <h5 class="mt-3">Navigation menu</h5>
                                <p>On the left side of your screen is the main navigation menu. It contains links to all modules like Shops, Collections, Expenses, and Reports. You can click the menu icon at the top to collapse or expand this sidebar.</p>
                                
                                <h5 class="mt-3">User profile & Logout</h5>
                                <p>In the top right corner, click on your profile picture to access your personal profile settings or to securely <strong>Logout</strong> of the application when you are finished working.</p>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 3. Dashboard -->
                            <section id="sec-dashboard" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">3. Dashboard</h3>
                                <p>The Dashboard gives you an instant snapshot of your business finances.</p>
                                
                                <h5 class="mt-3">Understanding the Summary Cards</h5>
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Today's Collection:</strong> Total cash and online payments collected across all your shops today.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Weekly Collection:</strong> Total collections for the current week.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Monthly Collection:</strong> Total collections for the current month.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Grand Total:</strong> The overall collection recorded in the system.</li>
                                </ul>

                                <h5 class="mt-3">Collection Trends Chart</h5>
                                <p>A visual graph that displays how your collections are trending over time, helping you identify busy periods or seasonal drops.</p>

                                <h5 class="mt-3">Shop-wise summary</h5>
                                <p>A list ranking your shops based on their performance, so you instantly know which branch is generating the most revenue.</p>

                                <h5 class="mt-3">Dashboard filters</h5>
                                <p>At the top of the dashboard, you can select different months or years to view past performance data.</p>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 4. Shop Management -->
                            <section id="sec-shop-management" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">4. Shop Management</h3>
                                
                                <h5 class="mt-3">What is Shop Management?</h5>
                                <p>This module allows you to register and manage all physical branch locations of Shiv Amruttulya.</p>
                                
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Add a new shop:</strong> Click "Add Shop", enter the shop name, address, manager details, and contact info, then save.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Edit shop details:</strong> Click the yellow 'Edit' pencil icon next to any shop to update its address or manager.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Activate/Deactivate shop:</strong> If a shop closes temporarily or permanently, you can change its status to "Inactive" so it no longer appears in active dropdown menus.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Search shops:</strong> Use the top search bar to quickly find a specific shop by name or location.</li>
                                    <li><strong>View shop information:</strong> Click the blue 'View' eye icon to see full details of the shop.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 5. Grocery Item Management -->
                            <section id="sec-grocery-item-management" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">5. Grocery Item Management</h3>
                                
                                <h5 class="mt-3">Purpose of grocery items</h5>
                                <p>Before you can record purchases, you must define the items you buy (e.g., Sugar, Tea Leaves, Milk, Cups). This module acts as your master inventory list.</p>
                                
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Add grocery items:</strong> Create new items, specify their unit of measurement (kg, liters, boxes), and assign them to a category.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Update items:</strong> Fix typos or change categories using the edit button.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Manage item status:</strong> Deactivate items you no longer purchase so they don't clutter your purchase screens.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 6. Monthly Grocery Purchase -->
                            <section id="sec-monthly-grocery-purchase" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">6. Monthly Grocery Purchase</h3>
                                <p>Use this module to record stock purchased for the shops.</p>
                                
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Record monthly purchases:</strong> Log what was bought, how much it cost, and the quantity.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Select shop:</strong> Assign the purchase to the specific shop that received the goods.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Upload invoice:</strong> You can attach a photo or PDF of the bill/receipt for accounting purposes.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Search, Filter, Edit, Delete:</strong> Easily find past purchases and correct any data entry mistakes.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 7. Daily Collection -->
                            <section id="sec-daily-collection" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">7. Daily Collection</h3>
                                <p>This is where shop managers record the revenue generated at the end of their shift.</p>
                                
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Record cash collection:</strong> Enter the physical cash counted in the drawer.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Record online collection:</strong> Enter payments received via UPI, Card, or other digital methods.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Add notes:</strong> Add remarks for any discrepancies or special events (e.g., "Heavy rain, low sales").</li>
                                    <li><strong>View collection history:</strong> Review past entries to ensure everything was logged correctly.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 8. Expense Management -->
                            <section id="sec-expense-management" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">8. Expense Management</h3>
                                <p>Track money spent on daily operations to ensure accurate profit calculations.</p>
                                
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Expense categories:</strong> Expenses are grouped (e.g., Electricity, Salary, Maintenance) for better reporting.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Add expenses:</strong> Log the date, amount, category, and shop.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Upload attachments:</strong> Attach a photo of the receipt or voucher as proof of the expense.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 9. Reports -->
                            <section id="sec-reports" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">9. Reports</h3>
                                <p>The Reports module automatically calculates your data and presents it in easy-to-read formats.</p>
                                
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Daily & Monthly Collection Reports:</strong> See exactly how much revenue was generated on specific days or over a month.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Shop-wise Report:</strong> Compare the performance of different locations side-by-side.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Grocery & Expense Reports:</strong> Analyze where your money is being spent to identify areas for cost-cutting.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Export features:</strong> Every report can be filtered by date ranges and exported to Excel or PDF for your accountant.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 10. Franchise Management -->
                            <section id="sec-franchise-management" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">10. Franchise Management</h3>
                                <p>For administrators managing multiple franchise owners.</p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Add & View Franchise:</strong> Register new franchise owners with their personal and business details.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Manage agreement dates:</strong> Keep track of when a franchise agreement starts and expires.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 11. Website Enquiries -->
                            <section id="sec-website-enquiries" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">11. Website Enquiries</h3>
                                <p>The Website Enquiries module captures and displays enquiries submitted by visitors through the public Shiv Amruttulya website. This helps you stay on top of customer interest and partnership requests without missing a single lead.</p>

                                <h5 class="mt-3">Contact Us Enquiries</h5>
                                <p>When a visitor fills out the "Contact Us" form on your website, their message is automatically saved here. You can view the following details for each enquiry:</p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Name:</strong> The full name of the person who submitted the enquiry.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Email:</strong> Their email address for follow-up communication.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Mobile:</strong> Their contact phone number.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Message:</strong> The detailed message or question they submitted.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Date:</strong> When the enquiry was received.</li>
                                </ul>
                                <p>Use this list to respond to potential customers promptly. You can search and filter enquiries by name, email, or date to find specific submissions quickly.</p>

                                <h5 class="mt-3">Franchise Partner Enquiries</h5>
                                <p>People interested in opening a Shiv Amruttulya franchise can submit their interest through the website. These enquiries appear here with the following information:</p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Name:</strong> The potential franchise partner's name.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Email & Mobile:</strong> Contact details for reaching out to discuss the franchise opportunity.</li>
                                    <li><strong>City / Location:</strong> Where they are interested in opening a franchise.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Message:</strong> Any additional details or questions they have about the franchise program.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Date:</strong> When they submitted their interest.</li>
                                </ul>
                                <p>Review these enquiries regularly to identify strong franchise candidates and respond to them in a timely manner to grow your business network.</p>

                                <h5 class="mt-3">How to use this module</h5>
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>View enquiries:</strong> Navigate to Website Enquiries from the sidebar and select either "Contact Us" or "Franchise Partner".</li>
                                    <li><strong>Search:</strong> Use the search bar at the top to find a specific enquiry by name, email, or phone number.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Sort:</strong> Click on any column header to sort the data by date, name, etc.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Export:</strong> Use the CSV or PDF buttons to download the enquiry list for offline review or sharing with your team.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 12. User Management -->
                            <section id="sec-user-management" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">12. User Management</h3>
                                <p>Control who has access to the software.</p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Add & Edit users:</strong> Create accounts for new managers or staff members.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Assign roles:</strong> Choose whether a user is an Admin, Franchise Owner, or Shop Manager. This dictates what they are allowed to see.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Activate/Deactivate:</strong> Instantly remove access for employees who leave the company.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 13. Profile -->
                            <section id="sec-profile" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">13. Profile</h3>
                                <p>Manage your own personal account settings. You can update your name, contact number, change your login password for security, and upload a profile photo.</p>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 14. Settings -->
                            <section id="sec-settings" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">14. Settings</h3>
                                <p>The Settings menu contains system-wide configurations, API version information (used by the mobile app developers), and this User Manual for quick reference.</p>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 15. Search & Filters -->
                            <section id="sec-search-filters" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">15. Search & Filters</h3>
                                <p>Every list in the application has powerful tools to help you find data quickly:</p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Search Bar:</strong> Type a name, email, or number to instantly filter the list.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Filters:</strong> Use dropdowns to filter by specific dates, statuses, or shops.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Sorting:</strong> Click on any column header (like "Date" or "Amount") to sort the data highest-to-lowest or lowest-to-highest.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 16. Export Features -->
                            <section id="sec-export-features" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">16. Export Features</h3>
                                <p>On almost every table, you will see buttons for <strong>CSV</strong> and <strong>PDF</strong>. Clicking these will immediately download the data you are currently viewing so you can print it or share it via email.</p>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 17. Mobile Features -->
                            <section id="sec-mobile-features" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">17. Mobile Features</h3>
                                <p>This application is mobile-friendly! If you open it on your phone:</p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>The layout automatically adjusts to fit your screen.</li>
                                    <li>The navigation menu tucks away neatly behind a "hamburger" menu icon.</li>
                                    <li>Tables allow you to scroll sideways so no data is cut off.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 18. Best Practices -->
                            <section id="sec-best-practices" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">18. Best Practices</h3>
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Enter data daily:</strong> Do not let collections or expenses pile up. Log them at the end of every shift for accurate dashboard metrics.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Verify before saving:</strong> Always double-check cash and online amounts before hitting save.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Use attachments:</strong> Always upload a photo of expense bills. It saves time during audits.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 19. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) -->
                            <section id="sec-faq" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">19. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h3>
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>How to reset my password?</strong> Contact the Admin, or go to Profile > Change Password if you already know your current one.</li>
                                    <li><strong>How to add a new shop?</strong> Go to Shop Management > Add Shop, fill in the details, and save.</li>
                                    <li><strong>How to record expenses?</strong> Go to Expense Management > Add Expense. Enter the amount, date, and upload the bill.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 20. Troubleshooting -->
                            <section id="sec-troubleshooting" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">20. Troubleshooting</h3>
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Unable to login:</strong> Ensure your email is spelled correctly and caps lock is off. If it still fails, your account might be inactive.</li>
                                    <li><strong>Data not appearing:</strong> Check your filters. You might be looking at the wrong month or shop. Click "Reset Filter".</li>
                                    <li><strong>Attachment upload issues:</strong> Ensure your photo is a standard format (JPG, PNG) and not too large (under 5MB).</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <!-- 21. Contact & Support -->
                            <section id="sec-contact-support" class="mb-5 pt-3">
                                <h3 class="text-primary border-bottom pb-2">21. Contact & Support</h3>
                                <p>If you experience any software bugs or need technical assistance that is not covered in this manual, please reach out to our support team.</p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Support Email:</strong> support@codecrafterinfotech.in</li>
                                    <li><strong>Working Hours:</strong> Monday to Friday, 9:00 AM - 6:00 PM</li>
                                    <li><strong>Software Version:</strong> 1.0.0</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

